-- title:
--   For each prime p at most Q, p to the floor of log_p Q is at most Q
-- statement:
--   For every natural number $Q$ and every $p \in$ `boundedPrimes Q`, $p^{\lfloor \log_p Q \rfloor} \le Q$, where $\lfloor \log_p Q \rfloor$ is Mathlib's `Nat.log p Q` and `boundedPrimes Q` is the finite set of primes $p$ with $p \le Q$ (the elements of $\{0, 1, \dots, Q\}$ that are prime).
